<title>FRANCE: France's Caisse des Depots 96 profit jumps 90 pct.</title>
<headline>France's Caisse des Depots 96 profit jumps 90 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net attributable			 3,969  up	    90 pct</p>
<p>Note - Caisse des Depots et Consignations is a state owned financial institution. It gave the results in a statement. It said net banking income totalled more than 10 billion francs in 1996, up 32 percent, due mainly to an improvement in interest margins and real estate activity. Provisions for property holdings totalled 1.1 billion francs, bringing its provisioning rate to 64 percent, it said.</p>
</text>
